# Nightly backup of the course-project database (homework #15).
#
# Install with `crontab backup.cron`, or drop it into /etc/cron.d/ with a user
# column added after the schedule. The path is the deployment checkout, not a
# developer machine — cron runs with a minimal environment and no shell profile,
# so the absolute path and the explicit `cd` are both load-bearing.
#
# 03:17 and not 03:00: everything on a host is scheduled on the hour, and a
# backup has no reason to compete with all of it for the same disk.
#
# The wrapper is the same one every other data-layer command uses — the
# connection string comes out of the vault (homework #11), never out of a file
# next to the script. On a host without vault access, set SKIP_VAULT=1 and
# provide DATABASE_URL, exactly as README's ## Grading section does.
#
# This schedule is what makes the RPO 24 hours: everything written after one
# night's dump is lost if the database is lost before the next one. That number
# is measured and argued in RESTORE-DRILL.md.

17 3 * * * cd /srv/invest-api && bash scripts/with-secrets.sh dev bash scripts/backup.sh >> /var/log/invest-backup.log 2>&1
